            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a place, then the Kannada for a centre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಉಪನಗರ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಪನಗರ — upanagara — \"a suburb\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾವು ನಗರದ ಹೊರಗಿನ ಒಂದು ಉಪನಗರದಲ್ಲಿ ಮನೆ ಹುಡುಕಿದೆವು. nāvu nagarada horagina ondu upanagaradalli mane huḍukidevu. We looked for a house in a suburb outside the city."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಪ-, near or secondary, plus ನಗರ, a city."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಪನಗರ (upanagara) is borrowed from Sanskrit upanagara, \"a suburb\" (Monier-Williams), from upa-, \"near\", and nagara, \"a city\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
